WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
How often did you go to the doctor in Mossville, or did the doctor come to you?

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.120
How did that work?

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:11.700
We had to go to a little place in Mossville was called The Clinic.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:17.240
The nurse would come and they would . . . That's when I found out I was anemic.

5
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.180
Because we didn't have no money to go to no doctor, We did home remedies.

6
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.480
Earache, toothache, cut foot.

7
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.780
We did home remedies.

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.580
Where was The Clinic in Mossville?

9
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.780
Old Spanish Trail.

10
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.620
What home remedies do you remember using?

11
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:42.220
[laughs] If you cut your foot real bad, you would use fat meat,

12
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:48.180
put it on the cut, tie it up, and for whatever reason it would heal.

13
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.280
If you had a toothache, you would use clover.

14
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.800
It would ease the pain.

15
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.040
I'm doing it right now because my mouth is sore . . . rinsing it out.

16
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.280
Earache?

17
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.200
Olive oil.

18
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:10.320
Mom would blow smoke from her cigarette in my ear and somehow or another it would ease the pain.

19
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.420
That's the degree of my sickness.

20
00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.080
I was sickly with the sore throat, I always had a sore throat.

21
00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.540
Gargle with salt and water and something they call alum.

22
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.360
You don't swallow it, but it draws everything out.

23
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.300
I mean, you can feel the tightness, bitter.

24
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.980
Winter medicine for worms and disease?

25
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.600
Castor oil.

26
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.680
Worst time of your life.

27
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:47.700
It was a taste you could never get rid of, but they said you take the castor oil and you suck the lemon,

28
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.720
or you take the castor oil and you drink the orange juice.

29
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.920
We never had orange juice [laughs].

30
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:59.000
We only had the lemon. [laughs] That was a time we dreaded.

31
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.060
And what was castor oil used to prevent?

32
00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.350
To clean your body out for the winter [laughs].

33
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:07.420
Oh. [laughing] And you would drink the castor oil?

34
00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.180
Oh.

35
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.180
A tablespoon.

36
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:15.260
To the day I don't use . . . I don't even like . . . You know, lipstick is made with castor oil.

37
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:25.280
I smell mine before I buy it, [laughs] because if it smells like it, I don't want it because it makes me nauseous. [laughing]

38
00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.860
And so you mentioned you still use the clover for a toothache.

39
00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.840
Are there other home remedies that your mother taught you that you still use today?

40
00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.420
I still have an earache, olive oil.

41
00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.377
What else do I use?

42
00:02:35.377 --> 00:02:39.200
We're diagnosed with high blood pressure, my mom and whatever.

43
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:45.560
A dash of cayenne pepper and water kept in the refrigerator, drink it every morning.
